# What `gcloud run deploy --source .` uploads to Cloud Build.
#
# This exists for the same reason as .dockerignore, but the stakes are higher:
# .dockerignore controls what enters a local image, while this controls what
# leaves the machine. Without it, `--source .` would upload the 2.1 GB imaging
# archive and every per-patient CSV to Google Cloud Storage.
#
# gcloud will synthesize a .gcloudignore from .gitignore when this file is
# absent. That would happen to cover the patient data, but relying on an
# inferred file for that is not a good way to decide what gets uploaded to a
# third party -- so it is written out explicitly.
#
# Keep in sync with .dockerignore.

# imaging archive and source clinical data
COVID-19-NY-SBU/
covid-19-cxr-ny-sbu.zip
deidentified_overlap_tcia.csv*
patient_details.csv
metadata.csv
MIDRC-RICORD-*.xlsx
midrc-ricord-*.zip

# derived per-patient tables and saved arrays
visor_labels.csv
visor_cohort.csv
visor_manifest.csv
visor_manifest_split.csv
*.npz

# credentials
kaggle.json
.kaggle/

# not needed to build or run
.git/
.gitignore
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.DS_Store
.claude/
demo.html
calibration_*.png
